---
title: Mexican Chocolate Snickerdoodles
course: Dessert
tags: 
- Cookies
- Vegan
source: Vegan Cookies Invade Your Cookie Jar
cuisine: American
servings: 24
---

Preheat the oven to 350. Line #two large baking sheets{} with parchment paper.

== Topping ==
Mix the @sugar{1/3%cup} and @ground cinnamon{1%tsp} together on a large dinner plate. Set aside.


== Cookies ==
In a #medium-size mixing bowl{}, use a fork to vigorously mix together the @vegetable oil{1/2%cup}, @sugar{1%cup}, @maple syrup{1/4%cup}, and @plant-based milk{3%tbsp}. Mix in the @vanilla{2%tsp}. 

Sift in the @all-purpose flour{1 2/3%cup}, @unsweetened cocoa powder{1/2%cup}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, and @cayenne{1/2%tsp}, stirring as you add them. Once all the ingredients are added, mix until you've got a pliable dough.

Roll the dough into walnut-sized balls. Pat the dough balls into the sugar topping to flatten into roughly 2-inch discs. Transfer the dough balls to a baking sheet, sugars side up, at least 2 inches apart (they do spread). This should be easy as the bottom of the cookies should just stick to your fingers so you can just flip them over onto the baking sheet. Bake for ~{10-12%minutes}; they should be a bit spread and crackly on tops. Remove the cookies from the oven and let them cool for ~{5%minutes}, then transfer them to wire racks to cool completely. 